{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Closed the plateau question from source rather than another execution, and corrected my own measurement proxy. The in-memory snapshot store's Create replaces its single latest snapshot and List returns only that one, and the file-backed store used by the cluster helper reaps older snapshots per its retain count, so a stored-snapshot count is not an attempt counter; the observed 1→2→3 then flat sequence is therefore consistent with attempts continuing while the proxy stopped tracking them. I withdraw both the earlier per-interval wording and any inference from the flat tail. The defect is unchanged and still rests on the persistent spurious verdict (store_last=0 against snapshot_index=3 with applied_index=3 and should_snapshot=true in CheckRun a4a0cbfa094b4d1982032d9de0652861, sustained through every later sample) plus the redundant snapshot creation at the unchanged index that the count growth 1→2→3 in parsed indices 1-2 requires; cadence is recorded as unmeasured and future rate work must count attempts (for example the FSM's Snapshot calls), with the other limits (store-specific wrapped store_last, non-production 100ms interval, single in-process/in-memory execution, no safety effect claimed) retained.\"}"}}
